// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: a `u8[]` handed to a `std:array` generic. `vl check` exits 0 with no
// diagnostic at any severity and is the ONLY command that misses it — `vl build` writes the
// `.wasm` and then exits 1, `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl run` exits 1. The engine refuses
// the module at load —
//
//   (wasmtime) type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found (ref $type)
//
// (the two `$type`s are different heap types; the disassembler prints both by the same
// placeholder.)
//
// PRE-EXISTING, MEASURED IN THAT DIRECTION rather than inferred from the filing date.
// `std/array.vl`'s storage-type section has recorded it since #1927 as "Pre-existing and
// unpinned", but a record is not a measurement, so this program was run against master's
// PUBLISHED compiler (`scripts/fetch-seed.sh`, `seed-latest`) and against the branch's own
// build: `vl check` rc 0 on both, and the identical engine rejection at the identical byte
// offset 489 on both. So it is discovery, not regression.
//
// This file is the pin that sentence lacked, and it is here because the LAST member of the
// `@no-instantiate` class graduated: the literal-union BOUNDARY family closed all four of its
// directions, and `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s corpus tripwire needs a live member of the
// class or it is a test that reads nothing. Its `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` is this program.
//
// THE MECHANISM IS THE `u8` STORAGE TYPE, and it is NOT the literal-union family: `u8` is a
// PACKED array element with no value-position rep of its own (`tests/cases/arrays/
// error-u8-storage-only.vl` pins its five doors), and a generic call spells `u8` nowhere, so
// it takes none of them. The monomorphized instance is pinned from the argument's REP, which
// for a `u8[]` is the byte-array wrapper, while the instance's own `self.length` /
// `self[i]` lowering resolves the i32-list wrapper.
//
// THREE OUTCOMES, ALL MEASURED, and they are what makes this the sharpest specimen rather
// than a spelling of one bug:
//
//   const xs: u8[] = [1,2,3]  →  xs.indexOf(2)          → check-clean INVALID MODULE (this)
//   const xs: u8[] = [1,2,3]  →  xs.reverse()           → check-clean INVALID MODULE
//   a `u8[]` from `std:fs.readFile`  →  xs.indexOf(2)   → an HONEST emit refusal
//                                       ("monomorphize: unsupported argument type for `self`")
//   an EXPLICIT `u8` in a value position                → a loud CHECKER error
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member of
// the class — the instruction that file has carried through six specimens.
import { indexOf } from "std:array"

const xs: u8[] = [1, 2, 3]
print(xs.indexOf(2))
